{
    "background_story": "Spark was a prized lobster in the coastal waters of Maine, renowned for his succulent tomalley - the creamy, flavorful substance found in the body of a lobster. As a young crustacean, Spark was always a bit of an oddity among his peers, with a vibrant blue shell that seemed to shimmer in the sunlight. But it was his exceptional tomalley that truly set him apart. Chefs from top restaurants would vie for the chance to serve Spark's rich, buttery flesh, and foodies would travel far and wide to taste his legendary tomalley. Despite his fame, Spark remained humble, living a peaceful life on the ocean floor, surrounded by the coral and seaweed he loved. His legacy lived on, however, as the benchmark for the perfect lobster tomalley.",
